# Server package rules

## tRPC

- One router per domain in `trpc/routers/<kebab-case>.ts`, exported as
  `<name>Router`, and **registered in `trpc/root.ts`** — unregistered routers
  are unreachable (tRPC, REST/OpenAPI and the CLI share the root router).
- Tenant data ⇒ `protectedProcedure` + `resolveCallerOrganizationId` (see
  00-general). Access-check helpers live in `modules/application/org.ts`
  (`assertApplicationAccess`, `assertEnvironmentAccess`, `getServiceContext`).
- Input validation with zod on every procedure.

## Engine

- Domains live under `modules/<domain>/`; routers stay thin — logic belongs in
  modules, which are unit-testable (vitest next to the code, `*.test.ts`).
- Deployments go through the in-process queue (`modules/deployment/queue.ts`);
  never spawn builds directly from a router.
- Traefik config changes go through `writeAppTraefikConfig` /
  `removeTraefikConfig` — never hand-write dynamic YAML from feature code.
- Every docker/shell operation takes the local/remote duality:
  `execAsync` for the Nixploy host, `execAsyncRemote(serverId)` over SSH.
- better-auth schema (`db/schema/auth.ts`) must stay in sync with the plugin
  version — missing columns silently break flows (e.g. 2FA `verified`,
  `failedVerificationCount`, `lockedUntil`).
